ow dialogs, preview focus respects current operation and newer intent, production history and exact team pictures preserved. Native file controls retain paired colours, inherited typography and bounded targets. Still Media fits narrow dialogs; chosen, saved and authored Preview return only current operation-owned focus. Cancellation and newer input retire focus without changing original media or assignments. Historical observations do not establish these journeys on the final deployed source. The complete selection retains 196 unchanged preceding source paths plus 267 inherited publication, release-utility and skill paths; inherited integration is provenance, not new native media-control features.\n\nExact game source: `a7a4e2d7090e2fe9d1843d88b63bc334b95bf61e` (tree `8f81812d56299c2819ec083d919d9085a36d223c`).\n\nAll six source gates passed through the hosted exact-source workflow. Each of the two complete four-shard families passed 5,730 tests with zero failures, cancellations, skips or TODOs. Production reproduction/readiness and the ordinary build passed on the hosted source. Both hosted source families used Node 20.19.6. No local command gates are claimed by this qualification pipeline; earlier local P05 cohorts remain separately source-scoped corroboration. The full test suite and ordinary build use the actual hosted authority above; no duplicate local execution is claimed.\n\nThe separately authenticated hosted utility inspected the complete frozen original artifact. Its source archive matches all 10,769 tracked files and modes. Every one of the 690 game files matches its original manifest. Local assembly rehashes the retained original metadata and preserves exact runner member descriptors for the source and distribution payloads; it does not download or rehash the large originals locally. The attached evidence preserves the selected original qualification and source-scoped Native media controls and Preview focus observations, including retained earlier failures; it does not replace verification of this release after deployment.\n\nPredecessor: [v0.61.0](https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/releases/tag/v0.61.0). Before selecting or deploying v0.61.1 as current, preserve its immediate predecessor v0.61.0 as exact immutable published source/distribution/metadata in a capacity-admitted archive, and retain every earlier catalog entry and owner. The v0.61.0 source package is qualified at fc2c7af6b22c703cc3bb2c081579878b7510f667 / bf11a670ac53a31d58b79540650229160bacd486, but its publication and public acceptance are not established by this requirements record. Complete the ordered predecessor publications and their actual retention/public gates separately. Once available, bind actual published nine-asset/tag authority, archive repository/main/tree/run/deployment/status, original hosted receipt and inventory, full public byte reconciliation, and scoped native/root admission. No future archive allocation, tag object, release/asset IDs, deployment or accepted state is invented here. Complete the normal main publisher PR/merge, deployed byte verification and applicable native play/offline evidence. Source and attachment qualification alone do not establish public P05 acceptance.\n\nAt package assembly, public byte/play/offline verification is pending; acceptance is recorded separately after publication. Full P03/P05/P07/P18 remains incomplete. Modeled input, browser observations and physical-device qualification remain separate evidence categories.\n"}